// A guarded tower, which is the one shape that reaches the materializer's fast path — and
// until this grammar existed, nothing in tests/Snapshots did.
//
// Where a guard names a value, the reader builds while the text is still being read, and the
// walk that materializes at the end has to know what it already built. For the usual case — a
// guard at every level of a tower, each asking for the record it has just captured — the walk
// is skipped altogether and the record is built where it stands. That path is emitted only
// where a guard builds, the walk is divided into arms of their own, nothing is marked and
// nothing is recovered; SqlStandardParser and TransactSqlParser reach it and no snapshot did,
// so the whole of it could be rewritten without appearing in any diff a person reads.
//
// Three things here are load-bearing and none of them is decoration:
//
//   The tower is EIGHTEEN levels deep because the arms have to be methods of their own before
//   the fast path is emitted at all, and that asks for sixteen of them. A shorter tower reads
//   the same language and emits the ordinary walk, which is the defect this file exists to
//   stop: a snapshot that looks like it covers a path and does not.
//
//   The guard sits BETWEEN the inner value and the closing bracket, not after it, so that the
//   record it asks for is the newest one written. That is the condition the fast path turns
//   on.
//
//   A tail is read AFTER the bracket closes, so the bracket's record is not the last thing in
//   the log when the level above asks. That is what puts records below a later guard's mark
//   that the walk never proves built, and it is the case the watermark must not claim.
//
// The language is arithmetic and uninteresting on purpose: `((1)#2)#3` and nothing else. What
// is worth reading is the file beside it.

trivia = { ' '* }

Tower : @int = level: L01 => @(level)

L01 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L02 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L02 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L03 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L03 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L04 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L04 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L05 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L05 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L06 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L06 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L07 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L07 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L08 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L08 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L09 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L09 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L10 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L10 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L11 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L11 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L12 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L12 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L13 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L13 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L14 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L14 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L15 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L15 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L16 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L16 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L17 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L17 : @int
	= '(' & inner: L18 & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                     => @(leaf)

L18 : @int
	= '(' & inner: Digits & when @(inner >= 0) & ')' & '#' & tail: Digits => @(inner + tail)
	| leaf: Digits                                                        => @(leaf)

Digits : @int = text: ['0'..'9']+ => @(int.Parse(text))

parse Tower
